• Here, \(\mathbb{Z}\) represents infinite free directions (the "rank" or basis), while \(\mathbb{Z}/p^k\mathbb{Z}\) represents finite cyclic "torsion" pieces built directly out of prime powers.

C. Cosmic Matter \(\rightarrow \) Elementary Particles & Symmetry Groups

In physics, atoms decompose into protons, neutrons, and electrons, which further decompose into 17 elementary particles (6 quarks, 6 leptons, 4 gauge bosons, and the Higgs boson):
• Group Theory Bridge: Physics actually uses abstract algebra directly here. Elementary particles are classified as irreducible representations (the "atomic" building blocks) of continuous symmetry groups (Lie groups), specifically the Standard Model gauge group \(SU(3) \times SU(2) \times U(1)\).
